==German==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|Turtel|Taube|t1=[[turtle#Etymology_2|turtle]] (= [[turtledove]], [[turtle-dove]], [[turtle dove]])|t2=dove, pigeon|lang=de}}, from {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|turteltūbe}}, {{m|gmh|türteltūbe}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|turtulatūba}}, {{m|goh|turtultūba}}, {{m|goh|turtiltūba}}, from {{etyl|ML.|de}} {{m|la|tortella}}, {{m|la|turtella}} (two [[Middle Latin]] [[diminutive]] forms), from {{etyl|la|de}} {{m|la|turtur}} (an [[onomatopoeic]] word imitative of the dove’s call, i.e., its [[coo]] or [[cooing]]).

===Noun===
